# A model small enough to commit, shaped to exercise what a model path has to survive (F136).
#
# Two `usemtl` groups, so it arrives as two PARTS rather than one draw — the property spec 124 cares
# about and the reason Sponza's 393 parts are the interesting number. Positions, normals and texture
# coordinates, triangles and one quad, because obj.c reads all of those and a fixture that only used
# triangles would leave the quad path untested by anything committed.
#
# Not a stand-in for Sponza: that is a real model a person points the view at, and a gate may not
# depend on a local asset. This is the smallest thing that proves the .obj path end to end.
v -1 0 -1
v  1 0 -1
v  1 0  1
v -1 0  1
v  0 1.5 0
vn 0 1 0
vn 0 0.4472 -0.8944
vn 0.8944 0.4472 0
vt 0 0
vt 1 0
vt 1 1
vt 0 1
usemtl floor
f 1/1/1 2/2/1 3/3/1 4/4/1
usemtl sides
f 1/1/2 2/2/2 5/3/2
f 2/2/3 3/3/3 5/4/3
